{"path": "repos/lablab-ai/community-content/pulls/1069", "status": 200, "data": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lablab-ai/community-content/pulls/1069", "id": 4516577593, "node_id": "PR_kwDOJcIRwc8AAAABDTWBOQ", "html_url": "https://github.com/lablab-ai/community-content/pull/1069", "diff_url": "https://github.com/lablab-ai/community-content/pull/1069.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/lablab-ai/community-content/pull/1069.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lablab-ai/community-content/issues/1069", "number": 1069, "state": "open", "locked": false, "title": "Add comprehensive Vectara Chat tutorial", "user": {"login": "Furox-Art", "id": 177975472, "node_id": "U_kgDOCpuwsA", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177975472?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art", "html_url": "https://github.com/Furox-Art", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR adds a comprehensive, hands-on tutorial for **Vectara Chat** for bounty issue #462. It teaches readers how to build a complete grounded chat experience with Vectara in Python, written in the first-person tutorial style used across the repo.\n\n**File:** `tutorials/en/vectara-chat-tutorial-build-a-grounded-chatbot-with-citations-in-python.mdx` (~2,800 words)\n\n## What the tutorial covers\n\nFollowing the structure recommended in the issue:\n\n- **Introduction to Vectara Chat** \u2014 grounded generation (RAG), numbered citations `[1]`, conversation memory, and the factual consistency score; links to the required [Vectara Beginner App Tutorial](https://lablab.ai/t/vectara-beginner-app-tutorial-showcase-the-creation-of-vectara-app-in-legal-use-case) and [Vectara Advanced App Tutorial](https://lablab.ai/t/vectara-advanced-app-tutorial-showcase-the-creation-of-vectara-app-in-legal-or-customer-support-use-case)\n- **Getting Started with Vectara Chat** \u2014 account + personal API key via the Console, `VECTARA_API_KEY` environment variable, virtualenv, `pip install vectara`, and creating a first corpus with `client.corpora.create`\n- **Building a Chatbot with Vectara** \u2014 ingestion with `CoreDocument` / `client.upload.file` (PDFs), single-shot grounded Q&A with `client.query`, printing `[1]`-style citations mapped to `search_results`, and multi-turn memory with `create_chat_session` + `ChatParameters(store=True)`\n- **Enhancing Chatbot Intelligence** \u2014 `lexical_interpolation`, `context_configuration`, reranking (`CustomerSpecificReranker`), `response_language` (ISO 639-3), `max_used_search_results`, `max_response_characters`, `generation_preset_name` (Mockingbird), `CitationParameters`, factual consistency gating, and streaming with `query_stream`\n- **Deploying and Testing Chatbots** \u2014 a complete runnable Streamlit `app.py` using the chat session, three concrete test cases (grounded / follow-up / out-of-scope), and deployment with `requirements.txt` + Streamlit Community Cloud\n- **Conclusion and Tips for Hackathon Participants** \u2014 recap, use-case ideas, and practical tips (show citations, protect API keys)\n\n## How API accuracy was verified\n\nAll code and parameters were checked against official, current sources before writing:\n\n- Vectara REST API v1\u2192v2 migration guide (endpoints, `corpus_key`, `response_language` codes): https://docs.vectara.com/docs/migration-guide-api-v2\n- Grounded generation / RAG overview (citations, Mockingbird): https://docs.vectara.com/docs/learn/grounded-generation/grounded-generation-overview\n- Official quickstart (`VECTARA_API_KEY`, `x-api-key` auth, Mockingbird preset, `[1], [2]` citations, factual consistency score): https://docs.vectara.com/docs/quickstart\n- API key management (`x-api-key` header, permission profiles): https://docs.vectara.com/docs/security/authentication/api-key-management\n- Console chat overview (chat toggle, chat history corpus): https://docs.vectara.com/docs/console-ui/vectara-chat-overview\n- Python SDK chat guide (`create_chat_session`, `session.chat`, `ChatParameters`): https://docs.vectara.com/docs/sdk/python/chats\n- Query API reference (generation config, citations styles): https://docs.vectara.com/docs/rest-api/query\n- File upload endpoint (`POST /v2/corpora/{corpus_key}/upload_file`): Vectara REST API v2 reference\n- Official `vectara` SDK (PyPI, v0.4.3): https://pypi.org/project/vectara/ and https://github.com/vectara/python-sdk\n\nAdditionally, every SDK class, field name, and method signature used in the tutorial (`SearchCorporaParameters`, `KeyedSearchCorpus`, `ContextConfiguration`, `CustomerSpecificReranker`, `GenerationParameters`, `CitationParameters`, `ChatParameters`, `QueryFullResponse.summary/search_results/factual_consistency_score`, `CreateTurnsChatsResponse.chat_id/answer/turn_id`, `client.query`, `client.query_stream`, `client.create_chat_session`, `session.chat`, `client.corpora.create`, `client.documents.create`, `client.upload.file`) was verified against the installed SDK v0.4.3 locally, so all samples are runnable as written.\n\nNote: this tutorial intentionally uses the current v2 API / official Python SDK, which differentiates it from the existing `vectara-chat-essentials` tutorial in this repo that uses the older v1 request style.\n\n/claim #462\n\n> **Disclosure:** This PR was authored by @Furox-Art (AI-assisted). Happy to adjust anything.\n", "created_at": "2026-09-13T02:11:31Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-29T18:20:52Z", "closed_at": null, "merged_at": null, "merge_commit_sha": "3a265e180acfff5cbf657cad35b857e8bcdc7627", "assignees": [], "requested_reviewers": [], "requested_teams": [], "labels": [], "milestone": null, "draft": false, "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lablab-ai/community-content/pulls/1069/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lablab-ai/community-content/pulls/1069/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lablab-ai/community-content/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lablab-ai/community-content/issues/1069/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lablab-ai/community-content/statuses/3fa43b88766e0d47f92cfafc5e93dfdf9f58851a", "head": {"label": "Furox-Art:tutorial/vectara-chat", "ref": "tutorial/vectara-chat", "sha": "3fa43b88766e0d47f92cfafc5e93dfdf9f58851a", "user": {"login": "Furox-Art", "id": 177975472, "node_id": "U_kgDOCpuwsA", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177975472?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art", "html_url": "https://github.com/Furox-Art", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Furox-Art/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "pu